/**
 * @file LumexUtility
 * @brief Utility module, the foundation of the library: assertion, attribute,
 * keyword and constant macros, compiler, feature and OS checks, type traits,
 * stack text and core dumps, demangling, safe numeric comparison (with the
 * ordering classes of its three-way result), bit and byte order helpers, the
 * iterator range, the process id, a callback slot, the `identity` and `less`
 * function objects and the `index_sequence` family.
 * @details Link <tt>%lumex::utility</tt> (compiled library; it links
 * <tt>%lumex::math</tt>, <tt>%lumex::optional</tt> and <tt>%lumex::span</tt>).
 * Works from C++11. The umbrella also includes `bit/`, `cast/`, `mem/` and
 * `ranges/`. In them `count_leading_zeros`, `byte_swap`, `is_little_endian`,
 * `downcast`, `downcast_noexcept` and `bad_down_cast`, `get_nearest_to`,
 * `iterator_range` and `mem::as` (reads a value out of raw bytes; the result is
 * `std::optional` from C++17 and the optional of `lumex::optional` before it,
 * `mem::optional_t`) work from C++11.
 * `functional/` (`functional::identity`, `functional::less`) and `sequence/`
 * (`sequence::integer_sequence`, `index_sequence`, `make_integer_sequence`,
 * `make_index_sequence`, `index_sequence_for`) work from C++11: the standard
 * type where the library has it (`std::identity` with the C++20 ranges,
 * `std::less<void>` and the integer sequences from C++14) and a class of this
 * library below. `traits::meta` has the C++11 forms `is_pointer_to_class`,
 * `is_lvalue_ref_to_class`, `is_complete_type`, `preserves_cv`,
 * `is_derived_from`, `is_extractible` and `is_byte_like` of its concepts, and
 * `traits::string::is_string_convertible` the form of `StringLike`.
 */
